    <h2>What Is the Dairy Queen Turtle Pecan Cluster Blizzard?</h2>
    <p>Among Dairy Queen's permanent year-round lineup, the Turtle Pecan Cluster Blizzard® Treat stands out as the choice for mature, sophisticated dessert lovers. Instead of crushed commercial candy bars or baked cookies, this recipe draws direct inspiration from traditional confectionery "turtles"—combining whole roasted buttered pecans, velvety caramel topping, and rich chocolate fudge cone-dip pieces blended into DQ's signature vanilla soft serve.</p>
    <p>The culinary triumph of the Turtle Pecan Cluster is its textural richness. Whole pecans provide a deep, earthy crunch and natural buttery oils that cut through the sweet, ribbons of caramel, while the chocolaty fudge chunks shatter into delicate cocoa shards that melt slowly against the cold soft serve.</p>

    <h2>2026 Prices &amp; Calorie Counts Across All Cup Sizes</h2>
    <p>Because whole roasted pecans represent a premium agricultural commodity, the Turtle Pecan Cluster Blizzard sits in Dairy Queen's specialty treat tier (typically ~$0.50 above entry-level flavors like Oreo or Butterfinger):</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Mini ($3.99 · ~360 cal):</strong> A compact 6-ounce serving that packs plenty of whole pecan halves and caramel swirls for a light post-meal indulgence.</li>
      <li><strong>Small ($4.79 · 570 cal · 20g Fat):</strong> The most popular individual cup, offering the perfect ratio of nuts, fudge, and caramel.</li>
      <li><strong>Medium ($5.79 · ~790 cal):</strong> An abundant dessert portion generously loaded with pecans.</li>
      <li><strong>Large ($6.49 · ~1,150 cal):</strong> A heavyweight 21-ounce treat designed for serious nut and caramel enthusiasts.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Nutty Treat Face-Off: Turtle Pecan vs. Other DQ Nut Classics</h2>
    <p>If you crave nut-infused treats at Dairy Queen, here is how the Turtle Pecan Cluster compares to its peanut-powered counterparts:</p>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Treat Option</th><th>Mini / Starting Price</th><th>Small Cal</th><th>Key Nut &amp; Chocolate Profile</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Turtle Pecan Cluster Blizzard</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>570</td><td>Whole roasted pecans, warm caramel ribbons, rich chocolate fudge</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Snickers® Blizzard</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>500</td><td>Roasted peanuts, chewy nougat, caramel, milk chocolate coating</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Reese's® Peanut Butter Cup</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>600</td><td>Chopped peanut butter cups; saltier, intense chocolate-PB blend</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Peanut Buster Parfait</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$4.99</td><td>710</td><td>Unblended sundae layers: Spanish peanuts, hot fudge, soft serve</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

    <h2>Customization Hacks &amp; Allergy Precautions</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Request a Hot Fudge Swirl:</strong> Ask the crew to drizzle a pump of hot fudge along the inside walls of the cup before blending for an extra layer of warm-cold chocolate decadence (~$0.50).</li>
      <li><strong>Extra Pecans:</strong> Serious nut lovers can ask for an additional scoop of roasted pecans blended in or sprinkled over the top curl.</li>
      <li><strong>Tree Nut Allergy Advisory:</strong> This treat contains genuine <strong>tree nuts (pecans)</strong> along with milk and soy. Because DQ uses shared blending spindles, guests with severe peanut or tree-nut allergies should avoid blended Blizzards; opt for packaged Dilly Bars or pre-packaged treats.</li>
      <li><strong>Upside-Down Guarantee:</strong> DQ rules mandate that every Blizzard cup must be flipped upside down before being handed across the counter—or your next one is free.</li>
    </ul>

